Description: media keys and tray menu for Jabra headsets
 The multi-function button on Jabra headsets does nothing on Linux. The
 Link 380 dongle declares the relevant bits as Constant in its HID report
 descriptor, and the kernel skips constant fields, so no key code is ever
 allocated and evdev never sees the press.
 .
 Jabraw reads the raw hidraw reports instead and forwards the button to
 the active MPRIS player. It adds a StatusNotifierItem tray menu showing
 battery level and charging state, the current player and track, volume
 and mute for speaker and microphone, and output device selection, plus
 dialogs for device information and settings.
 .
 Paired over Bluetooth rather than through the dongle, the same data is
 read over RFCOMM. Devices are matched by vendor id, so models other than
 the one this was developed against may work.
